UPDATE companies SET description='Sander''s Sew-N-Vac + The Fabric Bin operates in Aberdeen, South Dakota. The business traces its roots to 1945 when Al Sander opened Sander''s Sew-N-Vac to sell Electrolux vacuums. In 1976 his son Greg Sander purchased the downtown main‑street store and continued the family proprietorship.

In the late 1990s and early 2000s Greg expanded into fabric retail, opening The Fabric Bin. Today the store carries hundreds of bolts of fabric alongside notions, pre‑cut kits, and sewing supplies. Day‑to‑day operations are managed by Shirelle Stadel, a ten‑year employee, with assistant manager Alesha Stadel supporting projects and live shows.

The business serves individual sewers, quilters, and crafters both locally and through its online store. Customers range from hobbyists seeking specific fabrics to beginners attending classes for guidance on projects.

The company emphasizes its multi‑generational family ownership and personal customer service, positioning itself as a community hub for sewing education and inspiration rather than a volume distributor.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fabric and sewing supply retail", "Vacuum sales (Electrolux)", "Sewing education classes", "Live video shopping events", "Online fabric and notion sales"], "industries": ["Retail fabric and sewing supplies", "Consumer sewing and quilting"], "materials": ["Fabric (various)", "Notions", "Pre-cut kits"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned proprietorship since 1945", "Weekly live shopping shows", "In-store sewing classes", "0% interest financing via Synchrony", "Hundreds of fabric bolts in stock"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1945 by Al Sander -> /", "Greg Sander purchased in 1976 -> /", "The Fabric Bin opened late 1990s/early 2000s -> /", "Located at 111 South Main St, Aberdeen SD -> /", "Family-owned proprietorship -> /", "Store manager Shirelle Stadel 10 years -> /", "Assistant manager Alesha Stadel 4 years -> /", "Hundreds of bolts of fabric -> /", "Weekly live shows -> /", "Sewing classes offered -> /", "0% interest financing via Synchrony -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Al Sander opened Sander''s Sew-N-Vac in 1945 selling Electrolux vacuums. Greg then expanded the business by selling Fabric; in the late 1990s/early 2000''s Greg opened the The Fabric Bin. Today the store holds over hundreds of bolts of fabric!", "founded_year": "1945", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sander-s-sew-n-vac-the-fabric-bin' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wayne-Sanderson Farms, headquartered in Collins, Mississippi, was formed from the combination of two longstanding poultry companies with humble roots. The business draws on over a century of industry experience, though a specific founding year is not disclosed.

The company operates as the nation’s third-largest poultry producer, employing more than 26,000 team members and partnering with over 2,000 family farmers. The company emphasizes efficient operations, resource conservation, renewable energy, and waste reduction as part of its sustainable impact commitments.

Concrete customer-facing examples include its designation as the “Official Chicken of the Southeastern Conference” and a partnership with LPGA professional Jenny Bae, whose family has raised chickens for the company for a decade.

