UPDATE companies SET description='Sauder Furniture and Design Studio operates from a 20,000-square-foot location in Roanoke, Illinois. The business traces its roots to 1907 when Grandpa Sauder founded the company, and it has remained family-owned across five generations.

The company functions as a full-service furniture store and design studio, offering in-stock furniture across six showrooms — including sofas, loveseats, chairs, recliners, sectionals, bedroom sets, mattresses, and dining collections. Beyond furniture, Sauder’s carries flooring lines such as carpet, hardwood, luxury vinyl plank, and tile, and provides measure-and-install services for both flooring and window treatments. An in-house design team consults with clients on space planning and product selection, while a professional installation crew handles delivery and setup.

Sauder’s primarily serves residential customers throughout Central Illinois and the broader Midwest. Homeowners work with design consultants like Mary Lou Littlejohn to furnish and remodel living spaces, while the installation team coordinates projects from flooring to window coverings. The store also stocks home decor, candles, and fashion accessories, catering to walk-in shoppers and design clients alike.

The company emphasizes its family-owned heritage and community focus as differentiators. Leadership describes great customer service as a tradition and a way of life, and the staff — many of whom are local residents — take pride in serving neighbors and friends. The combination of a large showroom, integrated design services, and professional installation under one roof is presented as a full-service experience that sets Sauder’s apart from typical furniture retailers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Interior design consultation", "Furniture retail", "Flooring sales and installation", "Window treatment installation", "Delivery and setup", "Measure and install services"], "industries": ["Residential", "Home furnishings", "Interior design", "Flooring"], "materials": ["Carpet", "Hardwood", "LVP (Luxury Vinyl Plank)", "Tile"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1907", "20,000 sq ft full-service store and design studio", "In-house design consultants and professional installation team", "Six showrooms featuring furniture, flooring, and home decor", "Measure and install services for carpet, hardwood, LVP, and tile"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1907 by Grandpa Sauder -> /about-us", "Family-owned business across five generations -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Roanoke, IL -> /about-us, /", "20,000 sq ft full-service furniture store and design studio -> /about-us", "Six showrooms with in-stock furniture -> /", "Flooring offerings: carpet, hardwood, LVP, tile -> /", "Measure and install services for flooring and window treatments -> /, /about-us", "In-house design consultants and professional installation team -> /about-us", "Serves residential customers in Central Illinois and Midwest -> /about-us", "Wade Sauder (5th generation) President and Customer Relations Associate -> /about-us", "Jeff Sauder (4th generation) Co-owner and Customer Relations Associate -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Customers in Illinois and the Midwest have discovered our unique 20,000 square foot full-service furniture store and design studio located in charming Roanoke, IL.", "founded_year": "1907", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sauder-furniture-and-design-studio' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Savant Manufacturing Inc. (SMI) operates from Kinder, Louisiana, where it was formally established in 1985 after founder Kevin Savant began building four‑wheeler racks in his backyard in 1978.

SMI runs a full‑service metal fabrication shop under one roof, offering laser cutting (including a 6 kW fiber laser), CNC press‑brake bending up to 12 ft wide, turret punching, plasma cutting, saw cutting, CNC milling and turning, drilling and tapping, robotic welding, and an automated powder‑coating line with chemical pre‑treatment. The facility also houses a FARO Arm CMM for inspection and uses SolidWorks and AutoCAD for design and programming. The company advertises capacity for “thousands of parts” and mass‑production runs, though specific floor space or headcount figures are not published.

The core market is the ATV/UTV accessory sector – front and rear racks, drop racks, floor boards, gun racks, stick shifts and similar parts – which SMI has supplied since its inception. Beyond that, the shop serves a broader base of prototype and production customers across the southern United States, leveraging a partner network for any processes not kept in‑house.

SMI emphasizes a multi‑stage quality system: every weld is checked by the welder, then re‑checked by the buffer and painter; painters are reviewed by packers; packers by shippers. The automated powder‑coat line, in‑house CAD/CAM capability, and the practice of custom‑fitting each new ATV model year are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting", "CNC press brake bending", "Turret punching", "Plasma cutting", "Saw cutting", "CNC milling", "CNC turning", "Drilling and tapping", "Robotic welding", "Powder coating", "PEM insert installation", "Sanding and deburring", "Pipe bending", "Plate cutting and forming", "Engineering and design (AutoCAD, SolidWorks)", "CMM inspection (FARO Arm)", "Custom tooling and fabrication"], "industries": ["ATV/UTV accessories", "General industrial manufacturing"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["FARO Arm CMM", "6 kW fiber laser", "Two turret punches", "Press brakes (up to 12 ft wide)", "Haas CNC machines", "CNC plasma cutter with scribing", "Robotic welding cells", "Automated powder coating system (wash, spray, bake)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Multi-stage quality checks at welding, painting, packing, and shipping", "Automated powder coating line with chemical pre-treatment", "In-house CAD/CAM design using SolidWorks and AutoCAD", "Partner network across the Southern US for outsourced processes", "Custom tooling and fixtures for repeat production"], "facts_used": ["Location: Kinder, Louisiana -> db", "Founder: Kevin Savant, started 1978 -> /about", "Formal establishment: 1985 -> /about", "Processes: laser cutting, bending, powder coating, welding, machining, punching, plasma, sanding, PEM inserts, drilling/tapping, saw cutting, engineering/design -> /services, /", "Equipment: FARO Arm CMM, 6kW fiber laser, two turret punches, press brakes up to 12'', Haas CNC, CNC plasma cutter with scribing, robotic welding, automated powder coat line -> /, /services", "Industries: four-wheeler/ATV/UTV accessories (racks, floor boards, gun racks) -> /about; wide variety of clients -> /services", "Materials: steel, stainless steel, aluminum -> / (posts: Machined Steel Handle, Aluminum Shock Connection, CNC Bending of Stainless Steel, All Aluminum Robotic Welding Jig, Custom Aluminum Cabinet)", "Quality system: multi-stage checks (welder, buffer, painter, packer, shipper) -> /about", "Differentiators: automated powder coat, in-house CAD/CAM, custom fit for new ATVs yearly, partner network -> /about, /services", "Company type: manufacturer (full service machine shop) -> /services", "No certifications, employee count, cage code, min order, export compliance, languages, social links found in INPUT"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a full service machine shop we manufacture, modify, and repair prototype and production parts for a wide variety of clients.", "founded_year": "1978", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='savant-manufacturing-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Second Chance Welding operates in Johnston, Rhode Island. The shop is owned by Andrew Quinn, who holds certifications across a range of material thicknesses. The business focuses on certified automotive rust repair, fabrication, and structural steel welding.

Work is performed both in-shop and on-site via mobile service, with labor rates of $100 per hour in the shop and $125 per hour for mobile work, plus materials. Minimum shop charge is $100 for up to one hour; minimum mobile charge is $500 for up to four hours. Estimates are free and offered Monday through Friday from 3 p.m. to 5 p.m., with appointments available for other times.

Second Chance Welding serves vehicle and equipment owners needing rust repair, fabrication, and structural welding.

