UPDATE companies SET description='Sensitron Semiconductor operates from Deer Park, New York. The company traces its heritage back more than 50 years as a manufacturer of high-reliability power electronic components, though a specific founding year is not disclosed.

The company designs and produces solid-state power controllers, motor controllers, space-level diodes and die, and a range of high-reliability power electronics. Its product portfolio includes high-power rectifier bridges, lightweight SiC and IGBT power modules, SuperClamp transient voltage suppressors, rotating rectifier assemblies, and solid-state power distribution units. Sensitron also offers screening and test services, up-screening of commercial discrete parts, and custom hybrid microelectronics assembly certified to MIL-PRF-38534 Class K. Part numbers such as the SCP-5282 series, SPM1 series, and SEPD series illustrate the breadth of its catalog.

Sensitron serves the defense, aerospace, space, and medical markets. Its components are used in commercial aerospace, launch vehicles, naval and missile systems, and industrial generator applications. The company''s rotating rectifier assemblies, for example, are built for aerospace and defense generators rated up to 1000 V, 120 A, and 27,500 RPM.

Sensitron differentiates itself through its QPL listings under MIL-PRF-19500 for JAN, JANTX, JANTXV, and JANS diodes, its AS9100 registration, and patented packaging technologies such as the High Strength SMD package. The firm emphasizes rugged, lightweight, and cost-effective solutions for switching power supplies, AC-DC rectification, power distribution, motion control, and transient voltage protection.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','MIL-PRF-38534 Class K','MIL-PRF-19500 (JAN, JANTX, JANTXV, JANS)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High power rectifier bridge design and production", "Motion control module design and production", "Screening and test services", "Up-screening/testing of commercial discrete parts", "Performance screening", "Serialization and statistical control", "Custom hybrid microelectronics assembly (MIL-PRF-38534 Class K)", "Custom packaging (chip on board, power conversion)", "EOL replacements (DMS)", "Solid state power controller design (single and multi-channel)", "Solid state relay and contactor controller design", "High voltage diode assembly", "Diode stack and bridge stack assembly", "Bare die supply", "SiC and IGBT power module manufacturing", "Transient voltage suppressor module manufacturing", "Rotating rectifier assembly manufacturing", "Motor controller manufacturing", "Intelligent power module manufacturing", "Linear voltage regulator manufacturing", "Bidirectional current limiter manufacturing", "Lightning strike protection module manufacturing", "MIL-STD-704 and MIL-STD-1399 compliant module manufacturing", "High power protection (MIL-STD-1275) manufacturing"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Space", "Medical", "Commercial Aerospace", "Space and Launch Vehicles", "Naval", "Missiles", "Industrial", "High Reliability"], "materials": ["Silicon Carbide (SiC)", "Silicon"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified to MIL-PRF-38534 Class K for hybrid microelectronics", "MIL-PRF