UPDATE companies SET description='Sequel Wire and Cable LLC was founded in May 2019 in Argos, Indiana, by four partners who aimed to build a significant player in the wire and cable industry. The founding group included industry veterans such as Rich Carr, who serves as founder and CEO of the OEM group, and Gary Yetman, executive chairman of Sequel Holdings.

The company specializes in the drawing and extrusion of insulated copper wire, serving both OEM and low-voltage markets. Its product range spans UL/CSA and SAE wire for applications including agricultural equipment, automotive, battery and EV charging, construction equipment, marine, welding cable, and photovoltaic cable, as well as low-voltage categories such as security, fire alarm, access control, and audio-visual systems. Operations are conducted from its Argos facility, though specific facility size and headcount are not publicly disclosed.

Sequel serves a broad spectrum of industries, including alternative energy, automotive, heavy-duty truck, construction, appliance, marine, and recreational vehicles. Its customer base includes OEMs in sectors such as electric vehicle charging, battery systems, and industrial equipment, as well as low-voltage contractors for security, fire alarm, and building automation systems.

The founders established Sequel with a focus on employing the latest technologies, hiring top talent, and maintaining an unrelenting focus on customer service. The company highlights its ISO 9001:2015 certification, Great Place to Work recognition, and "Made in USA" designation as markers of its commitment to quality and domestic manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','Great Place to Work Certified 2022-27','Made in USA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Drawing and extrusion of insulated copper wire", "OEM wire and cable manufacturing", "Low voltage wire and cable manufacturing"], "industries": ["Alternative Energy", "Agricultural Equipment", "Appliance", "Automotive", "Battery", "Battery Electric Power and Charging", "Construction Equipment", "Control Panel", "Electric Vehicle Charging", "Heavy-Duty Truck", "Home Wiring Panel Prep", "Marine", "Motorcycle", "Off-Road Vehicle", "RV and Trailer", "Water Heaters", "Welding Cable/Commercial Welders", "PV Cable", "Security/Intrusion", "Access Control", "Thermostat", "Fire Alarm", "Audio Visual and Sound Systems", "Landscape Lighting"], "materials": ["Copper"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management", "Domestic manufacturing (Made in USA)"], "facts_used": ["Founded May 2019 in Argos, Indiana by four partners -> /about", "Leadership team includes Rich Carr (Founder/CEO OEM), Gary Yetman (Executive Chairman), Jim Coleman (President/CEO Low Voltage), Kurt Hennelly (President), Denise Feece (COO/CFO), James Rothstein (CCO/President Low Voltage), Brian Meachum (EVP Engineering), Tiffany Austin (Dir. Product Management), Mike Frigo (Senior Advisor) -> /about", "Drawing and extrusion of insulated copper wire -> /", "Markets served: Agricultural Equipment, Appliance, Automotive, Battery, Battery Electric Power and Charging, Construction Equipment, Control Panel, Electric Vehicle Charging, Heavy-Duty Truck, Home Wiring Panel Pre