UPDATE companies SET description='SESCO, an electrical contract manufacturer, was founded in 1983 by David Souders in Mont Alto, Pennsylvania. Beginning as a small wire harness operation, the company has grown into a full-service manufacturing partner operating an 88,000-square-foot facility in Pennsylvania. It remains a small business serving customers across the United States.

The company designs, prototypes, and manufactures custom electrical assemblies, including wire harnesses, cable assemblies, control panels, and box builds. Its capabilities span engineering support, supply chain management, and new product introduction.

SESCO serves OEMs and industrial customers, with notable work in the defense sector producing electrical systems for the U.S. military. It also supplies UL 508A control panels and cable assemblies for data center applications. The customer base includes innovative companies requiring end-to-end contract manufacturing.

