UPDATE companies SET description='Sider''s Woodcrafting operates from a home-based workshop in Brewer, Maine. The company was founded in October 2015 by Bruce and Mary Graybill after the birth of their first child prompted Bruce to start making cutting boards as holiday gifts using a table saw and belt sander. What began as a personal project quickly expanded when a friend requested eleven more boards, turning the effort into a family-owned business.

The workshop produces handcrafted end-grain chopping blocks, cutting boards in various sizes, charcuterie boards, specialty shapes such as cribbage boards and guitar-shaped boards, and epoxy-resin coasters and clipboards. Each piece is made from a mix of domestic and exotic woods chosen to highlight natural color and grain, with epoxy accents using SUPERCLEAR epoxy. In its first full year of operation (2016), the shop completed just under 400 boards.

Products range from small cheese boards to two-foot-long "mega" cutting boards, with designs that double as functional kitchen tools and decorative items.

The Graybills emphasize that every item leaves their shop as a functional work of art, backed by a commitment to stand behind their craftsmanship. The business grew from a desire to create everyday objects that showcase the beauty of wood while maintaining a hands-on, small-scale approach.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handcrafted cutting boards", "End-grain chopping blocks", "Charcuterie boards", "Specialty shaped boards", "Epoxy coasters", "Epoxy clipboards", "Custom woodworking", "Wood selection (domestic and exotic)", "Hand sanding and finishing"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Domestic woods", "Exotic woods", "SUPERCLEAR Epoxy resin"], "equipment": ["Table saw", "Belt sander"], "volume": "~400 boards in first full year (2016)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handmade in a home-based workshop beside the owners'' house", "Combines domestic and exotic woods to highlight natural color and grain", "Uses SUPERCLEAR epoxy for resin accents and coasters", "Every product backed by a personal quality commitment", "Small-batch production with attention to functional art"], "facts_used": ["Founded October 2015 -> /about", "Family-owned business -> /about", "Founders Bruce and Mary Graybill -> /about", "Located in Brewer, Maine -> /about and db", "Handmade cutting boards, chopping blocks, charcuterie, specialty boards, epoxy coasters -> / and capabilities", "Uses table saw and belt sander -> /about", "First full year (2016) sold just shy of 400 cutting boards -> /about", "Products made from domestic and exotic woods -> /about", "Uses SUPERCLEAR Epoxy -> / and /about", "Team members listed (Bruce, Mary, Anna, Hazel, Ryia, Alex, Rebecca, Megan, Aaron) -> /about", "Online direct-to-consumer sales -> /", "Workshop beside house -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every product that we make is handmade from our small workshop beside our house in Brewer, Maine.", "founded_year"