UPDATE companies SET description='Sierra Components Inc. (SCI) was founded in 1992 in Minden, Nevada, as a small family-run business. The company began with only a fax machine, a flow hood, and several nitrogen boxes, and has since grown into a multi-million-dollar distribution and processing facility specializing in silicon wafers and bare die. The president and founder brings over 40 years of bare-die distribution experience and 42-plus years in the microelectronics industry.

Today SCI operates as a value-added processor and distributor for the microelectronics and semiconductor sectors. Its services include visual inspection to MIL-STD-883 Method 2010 and MIL-STD-750 Methods 2072/2073, element evaluation and lot qualification to MIL-PRF-38534D (Levels H and K) and MIL-PRF-19500, alternate sourcing for obsolete or unavailable components, and wafer processing such as SAW sorting, inspection, and wafer probing. The company also manages surplus inventory programs that guarantee customers at least 50 percent of book value. A partnership with Kooker Technologies extends the offering to component design, packaging, and substrate fabrication with fast turnaround times.

Its client base includes organizations needing MIL-STD and MIL-PRF compliant processing, alternate component research, and inventory recovery solutions.

The company emphasizes personal service—no automated attendants—and a commitment to the highest standards of quality, reliability, and customer attention. Its positioning as “large enough to accomplish the task, and small enough to deliver personal attention” reflects a deliberate focus on responsive, relationship-driven support.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Visual inspection per MIL-STD-883 Method 2010", "Visual inspection per MIL-STD-750 Method 2072/2073", "Element evaluation per MIL-PRF-38534D Levels H and K", "Element evaluation per MIL-PRF-19500", "Lot qualification per MIL-PRF-38534D", "Source Control Drawing (SCD) compliance", "Alternate sourcing and component research", "Wafer processing: SAW sorting and inspection to die form", "Wafer probing", "Surplus inventory management and consignment", "Component design and packaging (via Kooker Technologies partnership)", "Substrate fabrication (via partnership)"], "industries": ["Microelectronics", "Semiconductor", "Bare die distribution", "Silicon wafer processing", "Defense / Aerospace (MIL-STD qualified)", "Electronic components"], "materials": ["Silicon wafers", "Bare die"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No automated attendants; customers always speak to a live person", "Large enough to handle the task, small enough for personal attention", "Surplus inventory program returns at least 50% of book value", "Partnership with Kooker Technologies enables component design, packaging, and substrate fabrication with fast turnaround", "Staff with over 78 combined years of semiconductor industry experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 in Minden, Nevada as family-run business -> /about", "President/founder has 40+ years bare die distribution experience -> /about", "Staff has 78 combined years in semiconductor industry -> /about", "Multi-million dollar distribution and processing facility specializing in silicon wafers and bare die -> /abou