UPDATE companies SET description='Simcona Electronics Corporation was founded in 1962 by Louis Iacona and Simon Braitman in Rochester, New York. The pair opened an 1,800-square-foot loft opposite Kodak Park as a component distribution company. The business remains family-owned and operated, transitioning to second-generation leadership in 1999 and sole ownership under Marc Iacona in 2011.

Today Simcona operates as both an electronic component distributor and a contract manufacturer of industrial control panels. Its 130,000-square-foot footprint spans three facilities in Rochester and supports a staff of more than 70. The company maintains a network of over 200 component suppliers and offers build-to-print panel manufacturing certified to UL 508A and UL 698, with capabilities ranging from single prototypes to high-mix, scalable production runs. Services also include prototyping, design-for-manufacturing support, kitting, inventory management, and 100% functional testing under an ISO 9001:2015 quality system.

Testimonials reference clients in each of these verticals, and the company''s blog highlights fiber-optic applications for the oil and gas industry. Simcona primarily serves the eastern United States.

Simcona emphasizes long-term relationships and invests heavily in workforce development, requiring Lean Six Sigma belts for operations and engineering staff, along with project management and UL 508A certifications. The company cites its purpose-built facilities, AI-enabled sourcing tools, and a culture of caring, collaboration, passion, loyalty, innovation, and integrity as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL 508A','UL 698']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Build-to-print control panel manufacturing", "UL 508A certified panel building", "UL 698 certified panel building", "High-mix/low-volume production", "Scalable production runs", "Full documentation and traceability", "Prototyping and new product introduction (NPI)", "Fast-turnaround prototyping", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) recommendations", "Digital work instructions with 3D models", "Engineering support for control panel design and compliance", "Supplier network management (200+ partners)", "AI-enabled component sourcing", "Kitting and inventory management", "Global and domestic sourcing strategies", "100% functional testing", "Continuity and compliance testing", "ISO 9001:2015 quality management", "Customer audit support", "Electronic component distribution", "Industrial cable and wire distribution", "Custom cable assembly", "Supply chain management", "Warehousing and forecasting"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Healthcare", "Military/Defense", "Data Infrastructure", "Commercial Products/Entertainment", "Industrial", "Oil & Gas"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["UL 508A and UL 698 certified control panel manufacturing", "200+ supplier network for hard-to-find components", "Lean Six Sigma certified operations and engineering staff", "AI-enabled sourcing tools for pricing and availability", "100% functional testing on every panel"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1962 by Louis Iaco