UPDATE companies SET description='Siwek Lumber & Millwork Corp has operated in northeast Minneapolis, Minnesota since 1933. The family-owned lumberyard began as a local supplier of building materials and has remained under family ownership for generations.

The company stocks a full line of construction lumber, redwood (including Heart Construction grade), and cedar for outdoor projects such as decks, fences, and garden beds. It also serves as a distributor for exterior doors (including Andersen storm doors), Milwaukee power tools and accessories, and GRK fasteners. The yard offers custom cutting of lumber to size and runs a recycling program that diverted 153.55 tons of scrap building materials in 2019, achieving a 75.25% diversion rate.

Its customer base includes residential construction projects, decking and fencing specialists, and community organizations; for example, the company donated lumber and cutting services to Boy Scout Troop 9060 in Woodbury for an Eagle Scout project.

