UPDATE companies SET description='SkyWater Technology is headquartered in Bloomington, Minnesota. The company took shape in 2017 when it acquired the fabrication facility originally established by Cypress Semiconductor in 1991. Now a wholly owned subsidiary of IonQ, SkyWater operates as the largest exclusively U.S.-based semiconductor foundry with no foreign controlling interest.

SkyWater provides pure-play foundry services including wafer manufacturing, advanced packaging, heterogeneous integration, and technology development across three U.S. facilities. The Bloomington flagship fab runs 200 mm equipment in a 91,000 sq ft class 10 cleanroom supporting 90 nm and larger geometries. The Kissimmee, Florida site adds 200/300 mm advanced packaging in a 36,000 sq ft class 1,000/10,000 cleanroom. The Austin, Texas fab, acquired in 2025, brings 200 mm equipment, a 114,000 sq ft class 1 cleanroom, 30,000 sq ft of probe and test, and 65 nm+ capability.

The foundry serves fabless companies, integrated device manufacturers, OEMs, startups, government agencies, and research organizations across quantum computing, automotive, aerospace and defense, high-performance computing and AI, industrial, and biomedical markets. Its DMEA-accredited supplier status qualifies it for radiation-hardened and other mission-critical programs.

SkyWater differentiates itself through a collaborative Technology-as-a-Service model that aims to accelerate customers from concept to production, secure domestic supply chains, and support national technology leadership.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Semiconductor wafer manufacturing", "Advanced packaging", "Heterogeneous integration", "Technology development", "High-volume production", "Multi-project wafer (MPW) services", "Technology-as-a-Service (TaaS)", "Quantum device manufacturing", "Superconducting qubit fabrication", "MEMS fabrication", "Photonics fabrication", "Radiation-hardened (rad-hard) by process manufacturing", "Read-out integrated circuit (ROIC) manufacturing", "CMOS manufacturing", "Probe and test services", "200 mm wafer processing", "300 mm wafer processing", "90 nm+ feature geometry", "65 nm+ feature geometry"], "industries": ["Quantum Computing", "Automotive", "Aerospace & Defense", "High-Performance Computing & AI", "Industrial", "Biomedical"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["200 mm wafer processing equipment", "300 mm wafer processing equipment", "91,000 sq ft class 10 cleanroom with SMIF", "36,000 sq ft class 1,000 and 10,000 cleanroom", "114,000 sq ft class 1 cleanroom", "30,000 sq ft probe and test facility", "90 nm+ feature geometry capability", "65 nm+ feature geometry capability"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest exclusively U.S.-based semiconductor foundry", "Only U.S. foundry free of foreign controlling interest", "DMEA-accredited Trusted supplier", "Technology-as-a-Service (TaaS) engagement model", "Three domestic fabrication facilities with advanced packaging and heterogeneous integration"], "facts_used": ["SkyWater is a U.S.-based semiconductor manufacturer and foundry -> /", "Roots trace back to Bloomington facility established by Cypress Semiconductor in 1991 -> /about-us", "Acquisition of facility in 2017 -> /about-us", "Three facilities in Bloomington, MN; K