UPDATE companies SET description='Solid State Devices, Inc. (SSDI) has operated from La Mirada, California since its founding in 1967. The company began with a focus on hermetic semiconductor devices and assemblies for critical aerospace and defense applications, and over more than five decades it has become a pioneer in high-power and high-voltage semiconductor manufacturing.

Manufacturing takes place in a La Mirada facility that houses cleanroom microelectronics fabrication, wafer processing, assembly, and extensive test capabilities. The company supports both standard products and application-specific power devices built to customer source control drawings.

The primary customers are aerospace and defense programs, with engineering and procurement teams at prime contractors and subsystem suppliers. SSDI also provides end-of-life and DMS solutions, offering cross-references for devices from manufacturers such as Motorola, Texas Instruments, Microsemi, International Rectifier, and Semtech.

