rs of combined engineering experience from major semiconductor firms", "In-house wafer fabrication, package tooling, and HiRel screening to JANS level"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1967 -> /about", "Headquarters La Mirada, California -> db, /about", "Manufactures high-power/high-voltage semiconductors for aerospace/defense -> db, /", "JANS, ISO 9001, AS9100 certifications -> db, /quality", "700+ years combined engineering experience -> /about", "In-house wafer fabrication, assembly, test -> /capabilities", "Small quantity orders, material lot traceability, anti-counterfeit -> /about", "Cross-references for Motorola, TI, Microsemi, IR, Semtech -> /about", "GaN and SiC product lines -> /about", "Equipment list (belt furnaces, wire bonders, diffusion furnaces, TESEC 3000 ATE, etc.) -> /capabilities", "Testing standards (MIL-PRF-19500, MIL-STD-883, etc.) -> /capabilities, /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Manufactures high-power and high-voltage semiconductor products for aerospace and defense at its La Mirada, California facility.", "founded_year": "1967", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solid-state-devices-inc-ssdi' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Solid State Logic was founded in 1969 by Colin Sanders CBE in the village of Stonesfield, Oxfordshire, United Kingdom. The company began by building switching systems for pipe organs before Sanders established Acorn Studios and produced the first SSL console, the A Series, in 1976. The business moved its headquarters to Begbroke Manor in 1986, adding a 4,000 m² manufacturing facility that opened in 1988 and remains the UK headquarters today. A U.S. office is maintained in New York, New York.

The company designs and manufactures analogue and digital audio consoles, audio interfaces, DAW controllers, analogue outboard processors, and software plug‑ins for music production, live sound, and broadcast. Key product lines include the System T broadcast platform (S500, S400, S300), the L‑Series live sound consoles (L650, L550 Plus, L450), the Odyssey and Oracle studio consoles, the ORIGIN series, and the SSL 12/18 audio interfaces.

SSL serves music recording studios, live sound engineers, broadcast facilities, post‑production houses, educational institutions, and installed‑sound venues. Notable installations include Spiritland’s live mix facility in London, Shoreline College’s teaching studio in Seattle, and DVLP Academy’s training center. The company also supports OB and sports production, podcast and webcast workflows, and cloud‑based virtualised production.

SSL’s differentiation stems from a history of console innovation: the SL 4000 E Series (1979) introduced motorised fader automation (Ultimation) and the SuperAnalogue™ signal path; the 2000s brought hybrid consoles (AWS, Duality) that merged analogue summing with DAW control; and the System T platform pioneered native ST 2110 IP audio routing with automated NMOS discovery. The Odyssey console adds full analogue processing with console‑wide Instant Recall.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Analogue console manufacturing", "Digital console manufacturing", "Audio interface design and manufacturing", "DAW controller manufacturing", "Analogue outboard processor manufacturing", "Software plug\u2011in development", "Broadcast audio production systems (System T)", "Live sound console manufacturing", "Audio networking (Dante, MADI, ST 2110)", "Training and education services"], "industries": ["Music Production & Mixing", "Live Sound", "Broadcast Production", "Post Production", "Education", "Installed Sound", "Touring & Events", "Podcast & Webcast Production", "OB & Sports Production", "Cloud Production", "Virtualised On\u2011Prem Production"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SL 4000 E Series console", "SL 9000 J Series console", "System T broadcast platform (S500, S400, S300)", "Odyssey console", "Oracle console", "ORIGIN series consoles", "AWS \u03b4elta console", "Duality Fuse console", "L650 live console", "L550 Plus live console", "L450 live console", "L350 Plus live console", "L200 Plus live console", "L100 Plus live console", "TE2 Tempest Engine", "TE1 Tempest Engine", "UF1 controller", "UF8 controller", "SSL 12 audio interface", "SSL 18 audio interface", "Alpha 8 audio interface", "Bus Comp Classic processor", "Super 9000 processor", "Revival 4000 processor", "Pure Drive Quad processor", "Pure Drive Octo processor", "The Bus+ processor", "Fusion processor", "500 Series modules"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": 